var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"editors/venues/#Venues-and-maps","page":"Venues and maps","text":"Events only store address text. The data repository's venues.json caches a map position per address; the site reads it when it is built, and never uses the network.\n\nNew addresses are looked up in OpenStreetMap (Nominatim) by tangokalender geocode events, at most one request per second. When OpenStreetMap doesn't know the house number, Kartverket's address register is asked instead (\"source\": \"kartverket\"); it also understands abbreviations such as «Chr. Krohgs gate». The intake bot does this for every submission and adds venues.json to its pull request.\nAn event is only placed on a map when the match is precise (a house number, a building or a venue). Others appear in the list without a pin.\nAddresses that weren't found are stored as not found and are only retried with --retry.","title":"Venues and maps"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/venues/#Fixing-a-pin","page":"Venues and maps","text":"If a pin is wrong, edit the address's entry in venues.json: put the right lat and lon (from openstreetmap.org: right-click → «Show address», or from norgeskart.no), and set \"source\": \"manual\". Manual entries are never overwritten.\n\n{\"address\": \"Øvre Slottsgate 3, 0157 Oslo\", \"lat\": 59.9106, \"lon\": 10.7439, \"precision\": \"house\", \"source\": \"manual\"}","title":"Fixing a pin"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/workflows/#Workflows-and-upgrades","page":"Workflows and upgrades","text":"A data repository has three short workflows. Each calls a reusable workflow in this repository at the release it is pinned to, and runs the TangoKalender version that Project.toml pins:\n\nData repo workflow Calls When What it does\nvalidate.yml site-validate.yml pull requests, pushes to main tangokalender validate events: schema, unique ids, file locations; warns (without failing) about two events of one series with the same start.\npages.yml site-pages.yml pushes to main, nightly, by hand Builds the site and deploys it to GitHub Pages.\nintake.yml site-intake.yml an issue with label nytt-arrangement or rettelse is opened or edited Turns the form into event files and opens a pull request (see Submissions and review).\n\nThe nightly build runs just after midnight Norwegian time, so «today», past events and the embedded images stay right.","title":"Workflows and upgrades"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/workflows/#How-the-package-is-fetched","page":"Workflows and upgrades","text":"Project.toml names the package by its SSH address:\n\n[sources]\nTangoKalender = {rev = \"v1.1.0\", url = \"git@github.com:Tangokalender/TangoKalender.jl.git\"}\n\nLocally that uses your SSH key like any other git command. GitHub's runners have no key, so the reusable workflows rewrite git@github.com: to https://github.com/ before installing (the code repository is public).","title":"How the package is fetched"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/workflows/#Upgrading-to-a-new-release","page":"Workflows and upgrades","text":"Pkg.update() does not move a pinned version. Use Pkg.add with the new tag, here v1.2.0:\n\njulia --project=. -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.add(url=\"git@github.com:Tangokalender/TangoKalender.jl.git\", rev=\"v1.2.0\")'\njulia --project=. -m TangoKalender templates      # refresh the issue forms, in case they changed\n\nThen set @v1.2.0 in the three workflow files (Dependabot opens a pull request for those), and commit Project.toml, Manifest.toml, the workflows and any changes under .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE. The footer of every page says which version built it («Bygget med TangoKalender v1.2.0»).","title":"Upgrading to a new release"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/workflows/#The-issue-forms","page":"Workflows and upgrades","text":"The forms in .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE are generated from the templates in this package, because their field labels are what the intake parser reads. Never edit them by hand: change the templates here, release, and run tangokalender templates in the data repository.","title":"The issue forms"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/workflows/#When-something-fails","page":"Workflows and upgrades","text":"Pages or Validate fails right away, without jobs: GitHub couldn't load the reusable workflow. Check that the @vX.Y.Z tag exists in this repository and that the repository is public.\n«Instantiate» fails: the pinned tag doesn't exist, or Manifest.toml wasn't updated after changing the pin.\nThe intake run failed on an issue: edit the issue (any change) to start a fresh run; re-running the old run reuses the old commit.","title":"When something fails"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/bulk-edit/#Bulk-edits-with-tangoedit","page":"Bulk edits with tangoedit","text":"To change many events at once, such as cancelling a month, moving a series to a new venue or correcting a price, editors with write access use the command line in a clone of the data repository:\n\ntangoedit, a stand-alone program for Linux, Windows and macOS (Apple chips). Download it from the latest release, unpack it and run tangoedit/bin/tangoedit. Nothing to install.\nor, with Julia, julia --project=. -m TangoKalender edit … in the data repository (the same command).\n\nThe programs aren't signed. On macOS, remove the quarantine once with xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine tangoedit; on Windows, SmartScreen may warn («More info» → «Run anyway»).\n\nTo edit one event at a time in a form, finding it by search, there is also an interactive editor (experimental, needs Julia).\n\n(Image: tangoedit cancelling a weekly milonga for November (invented events))","title":"Bulk edits with tangoedit"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/bulk-edit/#1.-Find-the-events","page":"Bulk edits with tangoedit","text":"tangoedit milonga                                   # upcoming events containing «milonga»\ntangoedit milonga type:milonga venue:sentralen      # all terms must match\ntangoedit series:onsdagsmilonga --from=2026-11-01 --until=2026-11-30\n\nA plain word matches the id, title, series, organiser, venue, teachers, DJ or start time, ignoring case.\nkey:text searches one field: any event field, or the short names type:, teacher:, music: and org:.\nOnly upcoming events (ending today or later) by default; --from/--until set the dates, --all includes past events.\nA leading edit is ignored, so tangoedit edit milonga works too.","title":"1. Find the events"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/bulk-edit/#2.-Look-before-you-change","page":"Bulk edits with tangoedit","text":"--dry-run prints each change as key: old → new; --preview prints each event as a card, with the changes highlighted and the old value struck through. --json prints each event's file name and its JSON exactly as it is (or, with changes, as it would be written), so you can read the full text without opening the file:\n\ntangoedit milonga-social-2026-11-13 --json\n\nNone of them writes anything.","title":"2. Look before you change"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/bulk-edit/#3.-Change","page":"Bulk edits with tangoedit","text":"Add KEY=VALUE to the search:\n\ntangoedit series:onsdagsmilonga --from=2026-11-01 --until=2026-11-30 status=cancelled\ntangoedit series:fredagsmilonga venue.name=\"Kulturhuset\" venue.address=\"Storgata 1\"\ntangoedit series:nybegynnerkurs class_price_nok=250\ntangoedit milonga-x-2026-11-20 teachers='[\"A\", \"B\"]' dj=null\n\nThe value is read as JSON when it is valid JSON (250, null, [\"A\",\"B\"], \"text\"), otherwise as plain text.\nNested fields use dots: venue.name, translations.en.title.\nEvery changed event is checked before anything is written. If one is invalid, nothing is written, and an error while writing restores every file.\nChanging start to another date moves the file; the id stays.","title":"3. Change"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/bulk-edit/#4.-Create-repeating-dates","page":"Bulk edits with tangoedit","text":"repeat copies an existing event to new dates. Then you don't have to submit every date of a weekly milonga or a course again:\n\ntangoedit repeat milonga-x-2026-11-20 --every=week --count=8                       # the next 8 Fridays\ntangoedit repeat series:onsdagsmilonga --every=2weeks --until=2027-06-30            # continues the series\ntangoedit repeat series:practica --every=month --on=last-friday                     # last Friday of each month\ntangoedit repeat series:nybegynnerkurs --every=week --count=10 --except=2026-12-21..2027-01-03 dj=null\ntangoedit repeat milonga-x-2026-11-20 --on=2026-12-27 'title=Juledagsmilonga'        # one date, on any weekday\n\nThe search terms must find one event, or events of one series; then the latest one is copied. To copy a particular event, give its id. That matters when the latest date is a special, such as a Sunday Christmas milonga at the end of a Friday series: copying it would give Sunday dates (with --every) or its holiday title. repeat prints a note when the latest event is on another weekday or has another title than most of its series, and names a typical event to copy instead:\ntangoedit series:milonga-social --all                              # the series, with ids\ntangoedit repeat milonga-social-2026-12-18 --on=2026-12-04 dj=TBA  # copy a regular Friday\n--every=week, 2weeks, month, 3months, … Weekly rules keep the template's weekday. Monthly rules keep its day of the month and skip months that don't have it (the 31st). With --on= they use a weekday instead: 1st-monday, 2nd-thursday, last-friday, 2nd-last-sunday.\n--on=DATE (or several: --on=2026-12-27,2027-01-03) gives the dates directly instead of a rule, on any weekday. Use it for one extra date, such as a Sunday special of a Friday milonga.\n--count=N makes N new events. --until=DATE stops at a date. Without either, the dates run 6 months from today. --start=DATE sets the first possible date (the default is the day after the template).\n--except= skips dates, such as a holiday break: 2026-12-24, or 2026-12-21..2027-01-03 for a range. You can list several, separated by commas. Skipped dates don't count towards --count, so a 10-week course with a break still gets 10 dates.\nEach copy keeps the template's times. Summer and winter time are handled, so 20:00 stays 20:00. The copy also gets the id <series>-YYYY-MM-DD, status scheduled and first_seen today. KEY=VALUE changes every copy, as in step 3.\nDates that already have the event, or another event of the same series, are skipped, so running the same command again is safe, and a date that was added before the series was set isn't added twice. --dry-run, --preview and --json show the new events without writing anything.","title":"4. Create repeating dates"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/bulk-edit/#5.-Publish","page":"Bulk edits with tangoedit","text":"Commit the changed files and open a pull request. The Validate check runs, and the site is rebuilt once it's merged.","title":"5. Publish"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/api/#API-reference","page":"API reference","text":"The functions behind the command line. Names marked TangoKalender. aren't exported.","title":"API reference"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/api/#Site-and-build","page":"API reference","text":"","title":"Site and build"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/api/#Events","page":"API reference","text":"","title":"Events"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/api/#Bulk-edits","page":"API reference","text":"","title":"Bulk edits"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/api/#Intake","page":"API reference","text":"","title":"Intake"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/api/#New-cities","page":"API reference","text":"","title":"New cities"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/api/#Venues","page":"API reference","text":"","title":"Venues"},{"category":"type","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.SiteConfig","page":"API reference","text":"SiteConfig\n\nSettings for one city's site (site.toml):\n\nslug: short id (\"oslo\"), name: site name in titles and feeds (\"Tangokalender | Oslo\"), city: the city (default venue.city, texts, geocoding).\nsite_url: where the site is published, without a trailing slash; may have a path (https://tango.oslo.no, https://example.github.io/bergen). Every absolute URL derives from it.\nrepo_url: the data repo on GitHub; the issue forms (…/issues/new?template=…) are there.\nmap_center (lat, lon) and map_zoom: the map view when no event has a position.\ncountrycodes (and optional viewbox, \"lon1,lat1,lon2,lat2\"): Nominatim search limits for geocode.\nog_image: link-preview image file (absolute path; site.toml gives it relative to itself), nothing = the package's generic image.\ntexts: per language (nb/en/es), UI strings that replace the package's _T entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.SiteConfig"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.load_site","page":"API reference","text":"load_site(file=\"site.toml\") -> SiteConfig\n\nRead a site's settings. Throws ArgumentError naming the problem if the file doesn't match schema/site.schema.json.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.load_site"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.write_site","page":"API reference","text":"write_site(dir, events; today=Dates.today(), venues=Dict(), kwargs...) -> files\n\nWrite the whole static site. Per language (Norwegian at the root, English under en/, Spanish under es/, same file names): the three views (index.html = compact list, uke.html, kort.html), one page and one .ics per event (arrangement/<id>/index.html, arrangement/<id>.ics), kalender.ics, rss.xml, legg-til.html, om.html, bygg-inn.html and the embeds (embed/). Once, at the root: events.json, the old for-ki.html redirect, the spreadsheet template, llms.txt and the schemas. site (see load_site) gives the city, name and URLs; venues (see load_venues) gives map positions. kwargs go to render_events_html.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.write_site"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.render_events_html","page":"API reference","text":"render_events_html(events; view=\"cards\", site=false, lang=\"nb\", …) -> String\n\nOne calendar page. view is \"cards\", \"compact\" (dense list grouped by day), \"week\" (one week at a time) or \"map\" (map of the venues above the compact list; positions from the venue cache, see write_site(…; venues)). site=true (used by write_site) adds the view tabs, links to event pages, the feed links and the language switcher. lang is \"nb\", \"en\" or \"es\" (see src/i18n.jl).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.render_events_html"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.render_events_file","page":"API reference","text":"render_events_file(input, output=\"index.html\"; kwargs...) -> output\n\nRender the events in input (an events directory or a JSON array file) as one page with render_events_html and write it to output.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.render_events_file"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.render_event_page","page":"API reference","text":"render_event_page(e, events; today=Dates.today(), correct_url=correct_form_url(), lang=\"nb\") -> String\n\nFull page for one event; events is used to list the other upcoming dates in the same series. Links are relative to arrangement/<id>/ in the language's tree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.render_event_page"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.calendar_ics","page":"API reference","text":"calendar_ics(events; name=site_name(), today, lang=\"nb\") -> String\n\nA complete VCALENDAR (CRLF line endings, folded lines) with one VEVENT per event that has an id and a start. Text (titles, descriptions, labels) and event URLs are in language lang; UIDs are the same in every language.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.calendar_ics"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.event_ics","page":"API reference","text":"The single-event calendar file linked as «Legg i kalender».\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.event_ics"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.rss_xml","page":"API reference","text":"rss_xml(events; today, title=site_name(), lang=\"nb\") -> String\n\nUpcoming events (end day ≥ today), most recently added (first_seen) first, at most 100, in language lang.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.rss_xml"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.events_json","page":"API reference","text":"events_json(events; today=Dates.today()) -> String\n\nUpcoming events (end day ≥ today) in the stored format, sorted by start – a simple feed for developers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.events_json"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.today_svg","page":"API reference","text":"today_svg(events; today=Dates.today(), days=8, lang=\"nb\") -> String\n\nToday's schedule as a 600px-wide SVG in the list design. Contains days day groups (today and the following days); the embedded script shows the one for the current Oslo date, so the image stays right between rebuilds.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.today_svg"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.week_svg","page":"API reference","text":"week_svg(events; today=Dates.today(), weeks=2, lang=\"nb\") -> String\n\nThis week's schedule (Monday–Sunday) as a 980px-wide 7-column SVG like the week view. Contains weeks week groups (this week and the next); the embedded script shows the current Oslo week, so the image stays right between rebuilds.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.week_svg"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.load_events","page":"API reference","text":"Events from a directory tree (events/) or from a single JSON file holding an array of events.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.load_events"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.load_event_tree","page":"API reference","text":"All events under dir (every *.json file, sorted by path), each as a JSON.Object that keeps the file's key order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.load_event_tree"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.save_events","page":"API reference","text":"save_events(events, file=\"events.json\") -> file\n\nWrite one event, or an array of events, to file as JSON with 4-space indentation and a trailing newline (the format of the files under events/).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.save_events"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.save_event_tree","page":"API reference","text":"Write each event to its canonical file under dir (see event_path); returns the file names.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.save_event_tree"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.event_path","page":"API reference","text":"Canonical path of an event file: root/YYYY/MM-month/YYYY-MM-DD-id.json.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.event_path"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.create_event","page":"API reference","text":"create_event(; title, types=[\"other\"], kwargs...) -> Dict\n\nA new event as a Dict with title, types and any other keys given as keyword arguments (create_event(title=\"Milonga\", types=[\"milonga\"], start=\"2026-10-16T20:00:00+02:00\")). Nothing is checked; see validate_event.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.create_event"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.expand_weekly","page":"API reference","text":"Expand a weekly event (weekday, start_time, end_time) into one dated event per week, from from through until, skipping dates in except. Each copy gets id = \"<series>-YYYY-MM-DD\" and series (defaults to the template id).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.expand_weekly"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.oslo_offset","page":"API reference","text":"UTC offset in Oslo at local time t (\"HH:MM\") on date d: CEST from 02:00 on the last Sunday of March until 03:00 (CEST) on the last Sunday of October.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.oslo_offset"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.validate_event","page":"API reference","text":"Schema problems for one event, as a vector of messages (empty when valid).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.validate_event"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.validate_event_tree","page":"API reference","text":"Validate every *.json under dir (or the events of a single array file). Returns (file, message) pairs: schema issues, duplicate ids, and files not at their event_path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.validate_event_tree"},{"category":"type","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.Event","page":"API reference","text":"Event\n\nOne event as a struct. JSON keys are the field names, except $schema (field schema) and end (field end_). Read and write files with read_event/write_event; change fields with set_path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.Event"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.read_event","page":"API reference","text":"read_event(file) -> (event::Event, keys::Vector{String})\n\nOne event file as an Event, plus its keys in file order (so write_event can keep the order and the absent keys). Throws ArgumentError for keys the schema does not know.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.read_event"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.write_event","page":"API reference","text":"write_event(io, e, keys)\n\nWrite e as save_events does (4-space indent, trailing newline): first the keys in keys (the order the file had), then any other field that is not null. A file read with read_event and written back unchanged is identical.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.write_event"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.set_path","page":"API reference","text":"set_path(x, path, raw) -> copy of `x`\n\nSet the field at path (JSON keys, e.g. [\"venue\",\"name\"]) to raw, read as JSON or else as plain text and converted to the field's type. A null object on the way is created first (setting venue.name on an event without a venue gives a venue with only a name).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.set_path"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.check","page":"API reference","text":"check(e::Event) -> problems\n\nThe schema rules for one event, checked on the struct (no JSONSchema, so it compiles trimmed). The app also runs the full validate_event_tree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.check"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.check_event_tree","page":"API reference","text":"check_event_tree(root) -> [(file, message)]\n\nvalidate_event_tree on structs: every file reads as an Event and passes check, ids are unique and files are at their event_path. Used by the trimmed app, which has no JSONSchema.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.check_event_tree"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.find_events","page":"API reference","text":"find_events(terms; root=\"events\", from=today(), until=nothing) -> [(file, event, keys)]\n\nEvents under root that match all terms (strings or SearchTerms), sorted by start. from drops events that ended before it (nothing keeps past events); until drops events that start after it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.find_events"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.edit_events","page":"API reference","text":"edit_events(terms, edits; root=\"events\", from=today(), until=nothing, dry_run=false, tree_check=validate_event_tree) -> (edits, written, errors)\n\nApply edits (\"key=value\" strings or (path, value) pairs, see set_path) to every event find_events returns. Events that don't change are left out. Nothing is written when dry_run is set or any edited event fails check. Otherwise the files are written (and moved when start or id changed) and tree_check(root) runs, rolling back on problems (the trimmed app passes check_event_tree, which needs no JSONSchema). A bad key or value throws ArgumentError.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.edit_events"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.edit_main","page":"API reference","text":"edit_main(args; io=stdout, err=stderr, tree_check=validate_event_tree, render=styled_text) -> exit code\n\nThe edit subcommand. render turns lines of (text, face) segments into something printable: styled_text (StyledStrings) here, ansi_text in the trimmed tangoedit app, which also passes tree_check=check_event_tree. 0 = done (also when nothing matches), 1 = an edited event is invalid (nothing written), 2 = usage error. A first argument repeat runs repeat_main with the rest.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.edit_main"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.repeat_events","page":"API reference","text":"repeat_events(terms, rule; root=\"events\", count=nothing, until=nothing, start=nothing, except=[], edits=[],\n              today=today(), dry_run=false, tree_check=validate_event_tree) -> NamedTuple\n\nCopy the template (repeat_template(terms)) to the dates of rule (recurrence_dates): after the template's date, or from start, until until, or count new events; without either, until 6 months after today. edits (\"key=value\", see set_path) apply to every copy. Dates that already have the event (same id or file, or any event of the series that day) are skipped. Every copy must pass check; then the files are written unless dry_run, and tree_check(root) runs (rolling back on problems). Returns (template, keys, events, exists, excepted, written, errors, note), events as (file, event); note is template_note(template, series) when the latest of a series was copied.\n\nrepeat_events(terms, dates::Vector{Date}; root=\"events\", except=[], edits=[], today=today(), dry_run=false, …)\n\nThe same, on the given dates (any weekday) instead of a rule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.repeat_events"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.repeat_main","page":"API reference","text":"repeat_main(args; io=stdout, err=stderr, tree_check=validate_event_tree, render=styled_text, today=today()) -> exit code\n\nThe repeat subcommand (also tangoedit repeat …, through edit_main). 0 = done, 1 = a new event is invalid (nothing written), 2 = usage error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.repeat_main"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.repeat_template","page":"API reference","text":"repeat_template(terms; root=\"events\") -> (file, event, keys)\n\nThe event to copy: the only event matching all terms (past ones included), or the latest one when all matches share one series, or the latest of the series a series: term names exactly. ArgumentError otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.repeat_template"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.repeat_event","page":"API reference","text":"repeat_event(t, d; series, today) -> Event\n\nA copy of template t on day d: same times (offset recomputed for summer/winter time) and the same number of days between start and end, id <series>-YYYY-MM-DD, status scheduled, first_seen today and no verification or crawl dates.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.repeat_event"},{"category":"type","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.Recurrence","page":"API reference","text":"Recurrence(unit, n, nth, weekday)\n\nEvery n weeks (unit=:week) or months (:month). Monthly rules fall on the template's day of the month (nth=0) or on the nth weekday (1 = Monday) of the month, counted from the end when nth<0 (-1 = last).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.Recurrence"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.recurrence_dates","page":"API reference","text":"recurrence_dates(r, anchor; from, until=nothing, count=nothing, except=[]) -> (dates, excepted)\n\nDates of rule r on or after from, in step with anchor (the template's date: its weekday, day of the month and the phase of every-N rules). Stops after until or after count dates. Dates inside an except range go to excepted and don't count. Months without the day (the 31st) or the weekday (a 5th Friday) are skipped.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.recurrence_dates"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.event_card","page":"API reference","text":"event_card(e::Event; before=nothing, width=terminal width) -> AnnotatedString\n\nA compact terminal card of e, laid out like the web card: date and time, type chips (and AVLYST), price, title, venue, organiser/teachers/DJ/music, the start of the description, and id/series/links. With before (the event before an edit), every changed part is highlighted with the old value struck through after it, and changed keys that the card doesn't show get a «✎ key: old → new» line.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.event_card"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.event_line","page":"API reference","text":"event_line(e::Event; width=terminal width) -> AnnotatedString\n\nOne line per event for match lists: short date and time, types, title, venue and id, in columns.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.event_line"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.styled_text","page":"API reference","text":"Lines of segments as a StyledStrings AnnotatedString.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.styled_text"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.ansi_text","page":"API reference","text":"Lines of segments as text with ANSI codes (plain text when color is false).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.ansi_text"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.parse_issue_form","page":"API reference","text":"Split an issue-form body into heading => value. GitHub's _No response_ becomes an empty string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.parse_issue_form"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.events_from_form","page":"API reference","text":"events_from_form(fields; issue_url=nothing, today=Dates.today()) -> (events, errors)\n\nTurn parsed form fields into dated v2 events (one per week for «Gjentas: Ukentlig»). errors are Norwegian messages naming the form fields; events is empty when there are errors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.events_from_form"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.events_from_table","page":"API reference","text":"events_from_table(text; issue_url=nothing, today=Dates.today()) -> (events, errors)\n\nEvents from pasted spreadsheet cells (see the file header). Every row is checked exactly like the ordinary form (events_from_form), so field rules and Norwegian messages are the same; errors are prefixed with the row number.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.events_from_table"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.events_from_json","page":"API reference","text":"events_from_json(text; issue_url=nothing, today=Dates.today()) -> (events, errors)\n\nParse a JSON submission (one event or an array), validate it against the submission schema, and build stored v2 events: Oslo offsets recomputed, ids/series/metadata set by the bot. Errors are Norwegian.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.events_from_json"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.apply_correction","page":"API reference","text":"apply_correction(fields, root; today=Dates.today()) -> (updates, errors, changed)\n\nupdates is a vector of (old_file, new_event); changed lists (label, before, after) for the first target. Targets the event with «Arrangement-ID», or it and all later dates in its series («Denne og alle senere datoer i serien»).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.apply_correction"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.correction_url","page":"API reference","text":"«Rett opp» link: the correction form with only arrangement_id and the read-only «Nåværende opplysninger» prefilled. GitHub resets URL-prefilled fields when they are edited, so the editable fields are left blank (blank = unchanged).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.correction_url"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.submission_schema","page":"API reference","text":"submission_schema() -> JSON.Object\n\nJSON Schema (draft-07) for submitted events: a single event or an array of up to 60. Derived from schema/tango-event.schema.json; published at submission_schema_url().\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.submission_schema"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.init_site","page":"API reference","text":"init_site(dir; slug, city, site_url, repo_url, name=\"Tangokalender | <city>\", version=package version) -> files\n\nStart a new city's data repo in dir: site.toml, an empty events/ and venues.json, a Project.toml that pins TangoKalender version from CODE_REPO_GIT (SSH), workflows that call the package's reusable ones, Dependabot, the issue forms, a placeholder link-preview image, .gitignore and a README with the one-time GitHub setup. Refuses to overwrite an existing site.toml.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.init_site"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.write_templates","page":"API reference","text":"write_templates(dir=\".\") -> files\n\nWrite the issue forms for the current site into dir/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/ (overwriting the package's forms, leaving other files there alone).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.write_templates"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.load_venues","page":"API reference","text":"Read venues.json into a lookup dict (empty if the file is missing).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.load_venues"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.save_venues","page":"API reference","text":"Write the cache sorted by address (stable diffs).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.save_venues"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.venue_coords","page":"API reference","text":"(lat, lon) for an event whose address is in the cache with a precise or manual position, otherwise nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.venue_coords"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.geocode!","page":"API reference","text":"geocode!(venues, events; fetch=_nominatim, fallback=_kartverket, retry=false, pause=1.0, today=Dates.today()) -> (added, failed)\n\nLook up every event address missing from venues (normalised keys) with fetch (Nominatim), and with fallback (Kartverket, source: \"kartverket\") when that finds nothing or only the street. Manual entries are never touched; addresses stored as not found (precision: \"none\") are only retried with retry=true. Network errors leave the address out, so it is tried again next time. pause seconds between requests keep within Nominatim's usage policy.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.geocode!"},{"category":"function","location":"dev/api/#TangoKalender.validate_venues","page":"API reference","text":"Problems in venues.json (schema and duplicate keys), as (file, message) like validate_event_tree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"TangoKalender.validate_venues"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/new-city/#Start-a-new-city","page":"Start a new city","text":"A city is a GitHub repository with its events, its settings and three short workflows that call this package. tangokalender init-site writes all of it.","title":"Start a new city"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/new-city/#1.-Create-the-data-repository","page":"Start a new city","text":"Install the tangokalender app (Julia ≥ 1.12; ~/.julia/bin must be on your PATH), then scaffold the repository:\n\njulia -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.Apps.add(url=\"git@github.com:Tangokalender/TangoKalender.jl.git\")'\ntangokalender init-site bergen --slug=bergen --city=Bergen \\\n  --site-url=https://tango.bergen.no --repo-url=https://github.com/Tangokalender/bergen\n\nFile What it is\nsite.toml The site's name, city, addresses and map (see site.toml).\nevents/, venues.json Empty: one JSON file per event, and the geocoding cache.\nProject.toml Pins this package to the current release ([sources], over SSH).\n.github/workflows/ validate.yml, pages.yml, intake.yml: each calls a reusable workflow here.\n.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/ The submission and correction forms, filled in with the site's address and city.\n.github/dependabot.yml Weekly updates of the workflow versions.\nassets/og-image.png Link-preview image (a placeholder; see below).\nREADME.md These steps, for the people running the repository.\n\nThen install the pinned package once and commit everything, including Manifest.toml:\n\ncd bergen\njulia --project=. -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.instantiate()'\ngit init && git add -A && git commit -m \"Tangokalender Bergen\"\ngit remote add origin git@github.com:Tangokalender/bergen.git && git push -u origin main","title":"1. Create the data repository"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/new-city/#2.-One-time-GitHub-settings","page":"Start a new city","text":"Settings → Pages → Source: GitHub Actions. A repository that isn't <owner>.github.io is served at https://<owner>.github.io/<repo>/; site_url in site.toml must match, or set a custom domain (below). If the owner's <owner>.github.io site has a custom domain, the repository is served under that domain instead: in the Tangokalender organisation, whose root site is Oslo's tango.oslo.no, a bergen repository would appear at https://tango.oslo.no/bergen/. Give a new city in this organisation its own domain.\nSettings → Actions → General → Workflow permissions: Read and write, and tick Allow GitHub Actions to create and approve pull requests. The intake bot opens pull requests.\nLabels: create nytt-arrangement, rettelse and trenger-retting (Issues → Labels).\nBranch protection on main: require the Validate check. Give editors the Write role.\n\nPush a commit or run the Pages workflow by hand; the site appears at site_url.","title":"2. One-time GitHub settings"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/new-city/#3.-Make-it-yours","page":"Start a new city","text":"Set [map] center in site.toml to the city centre ([lat, lon]), so the map view opens in the right place.\nDraw the link-preview image with the city name: julia <path to TangoKalender>/bin/make_og_image.jl in the data repository writes assets/og-image.png (it reads site.toml).\nTexts that mention the city use it automatically. To change a text, override it under [texts] (see site.toml).","title":"3. Make it yours"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/new-city/#Custom-domain","page":"Start a new city","text":"Oslo moved from tangokalender.github.io to tango.oslo.no this way. Pick the address before announcing the site if you can.\n\nDNS at the registrar. For the domain itself (an apex such as tango.oslo.no): A records 185.199.108.153, 185.199.109.153, 185.199.110.153, 185.199.111.153 and AAAA records 2606:50c0:8000::153, 2606:50c0:8001::153, 2606:50c0:8002::153, 2606:50c0:8003::153; for www, a CNAME to <owner>.github.io.. For a subdomain (tango.example.no in a zone you run), a CNAME to <owner>.github.io. is enough. A CAA record, if any, must allow letsencrypt.org.\nVerify the domain for the owner: organisation (or user) Settings → Pages → Add a domain, add the TXT record GitHub shows (_github-pages-challenge-<owner>.<domain>), then Verify. Nobody else can then claim the domain on GitHub.\nRepository Settings → Pages → Custom domain: enter the domain and save. GitHub checks the DNS and gets a Let's Encrypt certificate (minutes, at most about a day). Then tick Enforce HTTPS. With Actions-based Pages the setting lives here; a CNAME file in the repository is not needed.\nOnly when https://<domain>/ works: in the data repository set site_url in site.toml, redraw the link-preview image (bin/make_og_image.jl, it prints the address), rerun tangokalender templates (the issue forms link to the site) and update the README; push, and the site is rebuilt with the new address.\n\nAfterwards GitHub redirects every https://<owner>.github.io/… address to the domain, including the owner's other Pages sites (for Tangokalender, this package's documentation moved to https://tango.oslo.no/TangoKalender.jl/). Most calendar apps follow the redirect for kalender.ics, and so do most feed readers, but give out the new addresses from then on. The calendar's event ids contain the host (…@tango.oslo.no), so subscribed calendars replace the events once on their next refresh.","title":"Custom domain"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/submissions/#Submissions-and-review","page":"Submissions and review","text":"Anyone with a (free) GitHub account can submit events; an editor reviews them before they appear. The site's «Legg til arrangement» page explains the routes for submitters.\n\nRoute Form For\nOne event «Nytt arrangement» A single event, or a simple weekly series («Gjentas: Ukentlig»).\nSpreadsheet «Nytt arrangement (fra tabell)» Many dates: row 1 the column names, row 2 what all rows share, the rest only what differs.\nAI «Nytt arrangement (JSON fra KI)» An AI assistant turns an event page into JSON, using the prompt on the site.\nCorrection «Rett opp» on each event Change or cancel one date, or all later dates in its series. A blank field means unchanged; - clears.","title":"Submissions and review"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/submissions/#What-the-intake-bot-does","page":"Submissions and review","text":"When an issue with the label nytt-arrangement or rettelse is opened or edited, the Intake workflow:\n\nreads the form and writes or changes the event files, checking the whole calendar; new dates of an existing series join it (see below);\nlooks up map positions for new addresses (venues.json);\nopens a pull request on the branch arrangement/issue-<number> with a summary, and comments on the issue.\n\nIf the form can't be read, the bot explains what's wrong in a comment and adds the label trenger-retting. When the submitter edits the issue, the bot tries again. The AI form accepts a few field names that assistants tend to guess (price, flyer, image, url, …) and renames them (price_nok, flyer_url, link); any other unknown field is refused, and the comment lists the allowed ones.","title":"What the intake bot does"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/submissions/#New-dates-of-an-existing-series","page":"Submissions and review","text":"A submitted event joins a series that is already in the calendar when it has the same title (or the same series id) and the same organiser or venue name. It then gets that series and the id <series>-YYYY-MM-DD, so a single new date of a regular milonga or practica shows up with its other dates. The bot's comment names the series («Legges til i den eksisterende serien …»). If a submitted date is already in the series, also under another id with the same start time, the bot refuses it and points to «Rett opp». Same title but a different organiser and venue stays a separate event.","title":"New dates of an existing series"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/submissions/#Reviewing-a-bot-pull-request","page":"Submissions and review","text":"Read the summary in the pull request and the changed files. Check names against the source, the times and the venue.\nPull requests opened by the bot don't start the Validate check (a GitHub rule), but the bot has already validated the whole calendar.\nMerge: the site is rebuilt within a few minutes. Merging also closes the issue.\nTo change something first, push to the pull request's branch, or merge and fix it with Bulk edits with tangoedit.","title":"Reviewing a bot pull request"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/architecture/#Architecture","page":"Architecture","text":"The package reads a city's data (site.toml, events/, venues.json) and writes a static site: self-contained HTML pages (inline CSS and JS), feeds and embeds. Julia string interpolation builds the markup; there are no templates.","title":"Architecture"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/architecture/#Data-flow","page":"Architecture","text":"events/**/*.json ─ load_events ─▶ Vector of JSON.Object ─▶ renderers ─▶ write_site ─▶ _site/\nissue body ─ parse_issue_form ─▶ events_from_form / _table / _json / apply_correction ─▶ event files\nevents/**/*.json ─ read_event ─▶ Event (struct) ─ set_path ─▶ write_event   (bulk edits)\n\nEvents are plain dictionaries (JSON.Object, which keeps the key order) everywhere except the bulk edit, which uses the typed Event struct.","title":"Data flow"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/architecture/#Context-in-scoped-values","page":"Architecture","text":"Three ScopedValues carry the context, so helpers need no extra arguments:\n\nValue Set by Holds\nSITE main, write_site (_with_site) The TangoKalender.SiteConfig: name, city, URLs, map, texts.\nLANG each public renderer's lang= (_with_lang) \"nb\", \"en\" or \"es\".\nVENUES write_site(…; venues=), the CLI The geocoding cache, so builds never use the network.\n\nNothing site-specific is hard-coded: use site_url(), repo_url(), site_name(), site_city() and the form-URL functions. A test fails on a hard-coded site URL.","title":"Context in scoped values"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/architecture/#The-site","page":"Architecture","text":"Views (src/render/html.jl): index.html (compact list), uke.html (week), kart.html (map), kort.html (cards). One page script filters the rows; the filter state lives in the URL.\nEvent pages (src/render/event.jl): arrangement/<id>/ with JSON-LD, link previews and a map.\nFeeds and embeds: kalender.ics and per-event .ics (src/ics.jl), rss.xml, events.json, the SVG images that pick the current day themselves (src/render/svg.jl), and an iframe list (src/render/embed.jl).\nLanguages (src/i18n.jl): Norwegian at /, English at /en/, Spanish at /es/, with the same file names. Every UI string is in _T in all three languages; a test fails on a missing one.\nSubmission pages (src/render/submit.jl, src/llms.jl): «Legg til», the AI prompt and llms.txt.","title":"The site"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/architecture/#Intake","page":"Architecture","text":"The issue forms' labels are the parser's keys, so the canonical forms live in templates/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/ and data repositories get rendered copies. parse_issue_form splits a form; the plain form, the spreadsheet (events_from_table) and the JSON route (events_from_json) all end in the same event rules, and corrections go through apply_correction. Times are always recomputed as Norwegian local time.","title":"Intake"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/architecture/#Bulk-edits-and-trimming","page":"Architecture","text":"src/eventstruct.jl, src/edit.jl, src/repeat.jl and src/render/term.jl implement tangokalender edit and repeat on the Event struct. That code is written so juliac --trim can compile it into the stand-alone tangoedit:\n\nkeys reach fields through generated if chains instead of lenses built from strings;\nfield types are passed as Val, and nested keys use one function per level instead of recursion;\ndates are parsed by hand;\nterminal output goes through TangoKalender.ansi_text instead of StyledStrings.\n\nKeep it that way and run bin/build_tangoedit.sh after changing that path.","title":"Bulk edits and trimming"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/architecture/#The-event-form-and-TangoTUI-(experimental)","page":"Architecture","text":"src/eventform.jl is the form behind interactive editors, independent of any terminal library:\n\nform_fields() lists the fields in order, with Norwegian labels and help and the allowed values of choice fields;\nfield_text and set_field read and write a field as the text an editor types, through set_path (dates, times with the Oslo offset, the end after midnight, video links, the other language);\nfield_problems maps check messages to fields;\nevent_search_text and search_matches are the list search;\nchanged_fields, later_in_series, later_in_selection, split_by_organizer (the guardrail: only the same organiser) and copy_fields apply one change to later dates;\nsave_form_event writes one or several events at once, all or nothing.\n\nTangoTUI/ is a separate package (its own Project.toml, TangoKalender by path, plus Tachikoma.jl) with the full-screen editor on that form. Tachikoma pulls in REPL and Pkg and can't be trimmed, so it stays out of TangoKalender's dependencies and out of tangoedit. Its tests drive the editor with key events and read the screen from Tachikoma's TestBackend; bin/make_tui_demo.jl uses the same screens for the animated demo (Tachikoma's export_svg). A trimmed interactive mode for tangoedit would reuse eventform.jl with a small terminal layer of its own (an earlier trim spike is on the experimental/interactive-tangoedit branch).","title":"The event form and TangoTUI (experimental)"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/cli/#Command-line","page":"Command line","text":"julia --project=. -m TangoKalender … in a data repository, or the installed app tangokalender …. Paths are relative to the current directory; site.toml there gives the site (or --site=FILE). Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 validation failed, 2 usage error.\n\nusing TangoKalender\nprint(TangoKalender.USAGE)\ntangokalender - build the tango calendar as one static HTML page\n\nUsage:\n  tangokalender [build] [INPUT] [OUTPUT]   validate, then render (default: events public/index.html)\n  tangokalender site [INPUT] [DIR]         validate, then write the whole site to DIR (default: events _site):\n                                           index.html (list), uke.html, kort.html, arrangement/<id>/ pages and .ics,\n                                           kalender.ics, rss.xml, … – in Norwegian, and again under en/ and es/ –\n                                           plus events.json, for-ki.html, llms.txt, schema/*.json\n  tangokalender validate [INPUT]           validate only (also venues.json, if present)\n  tangokalender geocode [INPUT]            look up coordinates for new addresses (Nominatim, then Kartverket) into venues.json\n  tangokalender from-issue BODY.md         apply a submitted issue form: new event(s) (form, «Tabell» or «JSON»), or a correction («Arrangement-ID»)\n  tangokalender init-site DIR --slug=S --city=C --site-url=URL --repo-url=URL [--name=N]\n                                           start a new city's data repo in DIR (site.toml, workflows, forms, …)\n  tangokalender templates [DIR]            write the GitHub issue forms for the site into DIR/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/\n  tangokalender edit TERM… [KEY=VALUE…]   find upcoming events matching all TERMs; list them, or set KEY=VALUE on all\n                                           of them (tangokalender edit --help)\n  tangokalender repeat TERM… --every=RULE  copy an event to new dates: weekly, every N weeks/months, or on the Nth\n                                           (last) weekday of the month (tangokalender repeat --help)\n\nINPUT is an events directory or a single JSON array file. Paths are relative to the current directory.\n\nOptions (all but edit and repeat):\n  --site=FILE          the site's settings (default: site.toml in the current directory, if there is one)\n\nOptions (build, site):\n  --no-validate        render even if validation fails\n  --title=TEXT         page title (default: \"Tangokalender | Oslo\")\n  --subtitle=TEXT      page subtitle\n  --submit-url=URL     target of the «Legg til arrangement» link (default: the repo's issue form; empty hides it)\n  --correct-url=URL    base of each card's «Rett opp» link (default: the repo's correction form; empty hides it)\n  --venues=FILE        coordinates for maps (default: venues.json if it exists)\n\nOptions (geocode):\n  --venues=FILE        the coordinate cache to update (default: venues.json)\n  --retry              also retry addresses stored as not found\n\nOptions (from-issue):\n  --root=DIR           events directory to write into (default: events)\n  --issue-url=URL      recorded as the events' source_url\n  --report=FILE        write a Norwegian markdown report (for the issue comment)\n  --today=YYYY-MM-DD   reference date for \"date has passed\" checks (default: today)\n  --outputs=FILE       append `pr_title=…` and `issue_title=…` (e.g. $GITHUB_OUTPUT) on success\n\n  -h, --help           show this help","title":"Command line"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/cli/#edit","page":"Command line","text":"using TangoKalender\nprint(TangoKalender.EDIT_USAGE)\ntangokalender edit - find events and change them in bulk\n\nUsage:\n  tangokalender edit TERM… [KEY=VALUE…] [options]\n\nTERM     matches events containing it in id, title, series, organizer, venue, teachers, dj or start (ignoring case);\n         KEY:TEXT matches one key only (series:esa-tandas, type:class, venue:Lindern, status:cancelled).\n         Several terms must all match.\nKEY=VALUE sets a key on every match. VALUE is read as JSON (250, null, [\"A\",\"B\"], \"text\"), else as plain text.\n         Nested keys use dots: venue.name=…, translations.en.title=….\nWithout KEY=VALUE, the matches are only listed.\nA leading `edit` is ignored, so `tangoedit edit TERM…` and `tangoedit TERM…` are the same.\n`tangoedit repeat TERM… --every=…` copies an event to new dates instead (tangoedit repeat --help).\n\nOptions:\n  --preview         show each event as a card (after the edits, changes highlighted); writes nothing\n  --dry-run         list the changes; writes nothing\n  --json            print each event's file as JSON (after the edits), exactly as it is or would be written;\n                    writes nothing\n  --from=DATE       only events that end on or after DATE (default: today)\n  --until=DATE      only events that start on or before DATE\n  --all             include past events\n  --root=DIR        the events directory (default: events)\n\nThe stand-alone tangoedit is the same command; see Bulk edits with tangoedit.","title":"edit"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/cli/#repeat","page":"Command line","text":"using TangoKalender\nprint(TangoKalender.REPEAT_USAGE)\ntangokalender repeat - copy an event to new dates\n\nUsage:\n  tangokalender repeat TERM… --every=RULE [--on=WHICH-WEEKDAY] [--count=N | --until=DATE] [KEY=VALUE…] [options]\n  tangokalender repeat TERM… --on=DATE[,DATE…] [KEY=VALUE…] [options]\n\nTERM     finds the template, as in edit (past events included): it must match one event, or events of one series,\n         of which the latest is copied (series:esa-tandas continues that series; an exact series name wins).\n         To copy a particular event, give its id. A note says when the latest is on another weekday or has another\n         title than most of its series (a holiday special).\nThe copies get the template's times (summer/winter time recomputed), id <series>-YYYY-MM-DD, status scheduled and\nfirst_seen today. Dates that already have the event, or any event of its series, are skipped, so running the same\ncommand again is safe.\nKEY=VALUE sets a key on every copy, as in edit (dj=null, price_nok=150).\n\nRules:\n  --every=week|Nweeks       every week, every N weeks (2weeks), on the template's weekday\n  --every=month|Nmonths     every month, every N months, on the template's day of the month (months without it,\n                            e.g. the 31st, are skipped)\n  --on=WHICH-WEEKDAY        with month rules: the Nth or Nth-last weekday instead: 1st-monday, 2nd-thursday,\n                            last-friday, 2nd-last-sunday (months without a 5th … are skipped)\n  --on=DATE[,DATE…]         instead of a rule: just these dates, on any weekday (2026-12-27); may be repeated\n\nOptions:\n  --count=N         create N events (dates in --except don't count)\n  --until=DATE      create events up to and including DATE (default without --count: 6 months from today)\n  --start=DATE      first possible date (default: the day after the template); the rhythm stays the template's\n  --except=DATES    skip dates: 2026-12-24 or a range 2026-12-21..2027-01-03, comma-separated; may be repeated\n  --preview         show each new event as a card; writes nothing\n  --json            print each new event as JSON, exactly as it would be written; writes nothing\n  --dry-run         list the new events; writes nothing\n  --root=DIR        the events directory (default: events)\n\ntangoedit repeat … is the same command.","title":"repeat"},{"category":"section","location":"#TangoKalender.jl","page":"Home","text":"TangoKalender builds tango calendars: static, searchable websites listing the milongas, practicas, classes and festivals of one city, in Norwegian, English and Spanish. Each city keeps its events in its own data repository; this package turns them into the site and handles submissions, corrections and bulk edits.\n\nCity Site Data repository\nOslo https://tangokalender.github.io/ Tangokalender/tangokalender.github.io","title":"TangoKalender.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#How-the-pieces-fit","page":"Home","text":"data repo (one per city)                     code repo (this package)\n  site.toml, events/, venues.json   ──uses──▶  reusable workflows: site-validate, site-pages, site-intake\n  .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE (forms)               TangoKalender (pinned in the data repo's Project.toml)\n  .github/workflows (3 short files)             issue-form templates, schemas, tangoedit binaries\n          │\n          ├─ issue form ──▶ intake bot ──▶ pull request ──▶ editor merges\n          └─ main ──▶ Pages build (also nightly) ──▶ https://<city site>/\n\nEditors only need write access to their city's data repository. The code is changed here and a city picks up a new version by moving the pin in its Project.toml (see Workflows and upgrades).","title":"How the pieces fit"},{"category":"section","location":"#Start-here","page":"Home","text":"Starting or running a city: Start a new city, site.toml, Workflows and upgrades.\nEditing events: Events (the file format), Submissions and review, Bulk edits with tangoedit, Interactive editor (experimental), Venues and maps.\nWorking on the code: Architecture, Command line, API reference, Development and releases.","title":"Start here"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/events/#events","page":"Events","text":"Every event is one JSON file in the data repository, named by its date and id:\n\nevents/\n  2026/10-october/2026-10-14-esa-2026-10-14.json     # <start date>-<id>.json\n\nEvery event has a date. A repeating activity (a weekly milonga, a course) is one file per date, all with the same series id, so the DJ, price or venue can differ from week to week.\nCancelled dates stay: set \"status\": \"cancelled\" instead of deleting the file. The site shows them struck through with «Avlyst».\nTimes are Norwegian local time with the offset: 2026-10-14T20:00:00+02:00 in summer time, +01:00 in winter. A date without a time (\"2026-11-20\") is fine for festivals.\nPrivacy: only information that is already public. Names of DJs and teachers only with their consent; never phone numbers or e-mail addresses.\n\nThe schema, schema/tango-event.schema.json, is published on every site (e.g. https://tango.oslo.no/schema/tango-event.schema.json). Add it as \"$schema\" in a file to get completion in your editor. tangokalender validate events checks every file, unique ids and file locations, and warns about two events of one series with the same start (usually one date entered twice).","title":"Events"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/events/#Fields","page":"Events","text":"Generated from the schema; only id, title, types and start are required.\n\nusing TangoKalender, JSON, Markdown\ns=JSON.parsefile(TangoKalender.SCHEMA_FILE); defs=s[\"definitions\"]; req=Set(s[\"required\"])\nfunction kind(p)\n r=get(p,\"\\$ref\",get(get(p,\"allOf\",[Dict()])[1],\"\\$ref\",nothing))\n isnothing(r) || return Dict(\"datetime\"=>\"date or date-time\",\"nok\"=>\"whole kroner\",\"text\"=>\"text\",\"url\"=>\"http(s) URL\",\"day\"=>\"date\")[split(r,'/')[end]]\n haskey(p,\"enum\") && return join((\"`$(x)`\" for x in p[\"enum\"] if !isnothing(x)),\", \")\n t=get(p,\"type\",\"\"); t isa Vector ? join(filter(!=(\"null\"),t),\"/\") : string(t)\nend\nnotes=Dict(\"id\"=>\"Lower-case letters, digits and dashes; part of the file name and the event's web address. Never change it.\",\n \"title\"=>\"As the organiser writes it.\",\"start\"=>\"`2026-10-14T20:00:00+02:00`, or a date for all-day events.\",\n \"end\"=>\"Same format. After midnight: the next day's date.\",\"venue\"=>\"`{\\\"name\\\", \\\"address\\\", \\\"city\\\"}`; `null` when not announced.\",\n \"organizer\"=>\"Group or person that organises it.\",\"dj\"=>\"Only with consent.\",\"teachers\"=>\"List of names; only with consent.\",\n \"price_nok\"=>\"Entry price.\",\"student_price_nok\"=>\"Reduced price.\",\"class_price_nok\"=>\"Class or course price (for a whole course: on every date).\",\n \"description\"=>\"1–3 short, neutral sentences.\",\"flyer_url\"=>\"Direct link to the image; used in link previews.\",\n \"video\"=>\"`{\\\"platform\\\": \\\"youtube\\\" or \\\"vimeo\\\", \\\"id\\\"}`.\",\"link\"=>\"The official event page.\",\n \"source\"=>\"Where the information came from (set by the bot).\",\"source_url\"=>\"Link to that source.\",\n \"published_date\"=>\"When the source published it.\",\"first_seen\"=>\"Added to the calendar (set by the bot).\",\n \"last_verified\"=>\"Last checked against the source.\",\"crawl_timestamp\"=>\"When it was read (set by the bot).\",\n \"confidence\"=>\"0–1: how sure the extraction was.\",\"music_style\"=>\"See the table below.\",\"translations\"=>\"Title and description in other languages: `{\\\"en\\\": {\\\"title\\\", \\\"description\\\"}}`.\")\nnote(k,p)=replace(isempty(get(p,\"description\",\"\")) ? get(notes,k,\"\") : p[\"description\"],\"|\"=>\"\\\\|\",\"\\n\"=>\" \")\nrows=[\"| `$k` | $(k in req ? \"yes\" : \"\") | $(kind(p)) | $(note(k,p)) |\" for (k,p) in s[\"properties\"] if k!=\"\\$schema\"]\nMarkdown.parse(\"| Field | Required | Value | Notes |\\n|:--|:--|:--|:--|\\n\"*join(rows,\"\\n\"))\n  Field             Required Value                Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \n  ––––––––––––––––– –––––––– –––––––––––––––––––– ––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––\n  \u001b[36mid\u001b[39m                yes      string               Lower-case letters, digits and dashes; part of the file name and the event's web address. Never change it.                                                                                                                        \n  \u001b[36mtitle\u001b[39m             yes      string               The event's own name, without the organiser, venue or date (\"Nybegynnerkurs i tango\", not \"Nybegynnerkurs i tango (Tango Puente)\"): \u001b[36morganizer\u001b[39m is shown next to it. Keep a name that is the event's real name, e.g. \"Otra Milonga\".\n  \u001b[36mtypes\u001b[39m             yes      array                One or more: e.g. [\"class\", \"milonga\"] for a class followed by a milonga, [\"milonga\", \"outdoor\"] for an open-air milonga (utetango).                                                                                              \n  \u001b[36mstatus\u001b[39m                     \u001b[36mscheduled\u001b[39m, \u001b[36mcancelled\u001b[39m Missing or null means scheduled. Mark cancelled dates instead of deleting the file.                                                                                                                                               \n  \u001b[36mseries\u001b[39m                     string               Shared id for all dates of a repeating event (weekly milonga, course).                                                                                                                                                            \n  \u001b[36mstart\u001b[39m             yes      date or date-time    \u001b[36m2026-10-14T20:00:00+02:00\u001b[39m, or a date for all-day events.                                                                                                                                                                          \n  \u001b[36mend\u001b[39m                        date or date-time    Same format. After midnight: the next day's date.                                                                                                                                                                                 \n  \u001b[36mvenue\u001b[39m                      object               \u001b[36m{\"name\", \"address\", \"city\"}\u001b[39m; \u001b[36mnull\u001b[39m when not announced.                                                                                                                                                                             \n  \u001b[36morganizer\u001b[39m                  text                 Group or person that organises it.                                                                                                                                                                                                \n  \u001b[36mdj\u001b[39m                         text                 Only with consent.                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n  \u001b[36mteachers\u001b[39m                   array                List of names; only with consent.                                                                                                                                                                                                 \n  \u001b[36mmusic_style\u001b[39m                array                See the table below.                                                                                                                                                                                                              \n  \u001b[36mprice_nok\u001b[39m                  whole kroner         Entry price.                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \n  \u001b[36mstudent_price_nok\u001b[39m          whole kroner         Reduced price.                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n  \u001b[36mclass_price_nok\u001b[39m            whole kroner         Class or course price (for a whole course: on every date).                                                                                                                                                                        \n  \u001b[36mdescription\u001b[39m                text                 1–3 short, neutral sentences.                                                                                                                                                                                                     \n  \u001b[36mlang\u001b[39m                       \u001b[36mnb\u001b[39m, \u001b[36men\u001b[39m               Language of \u001b[36mtitle\u001b[39m and \u001b[36mdescription\u001b[39m: nb (Norwegian, the default when missing) or en (English).                                                                                                                                      \n  \u001b[36mtranslations\u001b[39m               object               Optional title/description in other languages, e.g. {\"en\": {\"title\": …, \"description\": …}} for a Norwegian event. Only text the organiser provided – no machine translation.                                                      \n  \u001b[36mflyer_url\u001b[39m                  http(s) URL          Direct link to the image; used in link previews.                                                                                                                                                                                  \n  \u001b[36mvideo\u001b[39m                      object               \u001b[36m{\"platform\": \"youtube\" or \"vimeo\", \"id\"}\u001b[39m.                                                                                                                                                                                         \n  \u001b[36mlink\u001b[39m                       http(s) URL          The official event page.                                                                                                                                                                                                          \n  \u001b[36msource\u001b[39m                     text                 Where the information came from (set by the bot).                                                                                                                                                                                 \n  \u001b[36msource_url\u001b[39m                 http(s) URL          Link to that source.                                                                                                                                                                                                              \n  \u001b[36mpublished_date\u001b[39m             date                 When the source published it.                                                                                                                                                                                                     \n  \u001b[36mfirst_seen\u001b[39m                 date                 Added to the calendar (set by the bot).                                                                                                                                                                                           \n  \u001b[36mlast_verified\u001b[39m              date                 Last checked against the source.                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n  \u001b[36mcrawl_timestamp\u001b[39m            date or date-time    When it was read (set by the bot).                                                                                                                                                                                                \n  \u001b[36mconfidence\u001b[39m                 number               0–1: how sure the extraction was.                                                                                                                                                                                                 ","title":"Fields"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/events/#Types-and-music-styles","page":"Events","text":"types lists one or more of the values below, in the order shown on the site; a class followed by a milonga is [\"class\", \"milonga\"], an open-air milonga [\"milonga\", \"outdoor\"].\n\nusing TangoKalender, Markdown\nTK=TangoKalender\nMarkdown.parse(\"| `types` | Norwegian | English |\\n|:--|:--|:--|\\n\"*join((\"| `$t` | $(TK._TYPES[t]) | $(TK._TYPES_I18N[\"en\"][t]) |\" for t in TK.TYPE_ORDER),\"\\n\")*\n \"\\n\\n| `music_style` | Norwegian | English |\\n|:--|:--|:--|\\n\"*join((\"| `$m` | $(TK._MUSIC[m]) | $(TK._MUSIC_I18N[\"en\"][m]) |\" for m in sort(collect(keys(TK._MUSIC)))),\"\\n\"))\n  \u001b[36mtypes\u001b[39m    Norwegian English \n  –––––––– ––––––––– ––––––––\n  \u001b[36mclass\u001b[39m    Kurs      Class   \n  \u001b[36mworkshop\u001b[39m Workshop  Workshop\n  \u001b[36mmilonga\u001b[39m  Milonga   Milonga \n  \u001b[36mpractica\u001b[39m Practica  Practica\n  \u001b[36mfestival\u001b[39m Festival  Festival\n  \u001b[36mmarathon\u001b[39m Maraton   Marathon\n  \u001b[36moutdoor\u001b[39m  Utetango  Open-air\n  \u001b[36mother\u001b[39m    Annet     Other   \n\n  \u001b[36mmusic_style\u001b[39m    Norwegian        English          \n  –––––––––––––– –––––––––––––––– –––––––––––––––––\n  \u001b[36malternative\u001b[39m    Alternativ / neo Alternative / neo\n  \u001b[36mlive_orchestra\u001b[39m Levende orkester Live orchestra   \n  \u001b[36mtraditional\u001b[39m    Tradisjonell     Traditional      ","title":"Types and music styles"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/site-config/#site-config","page":"site.toml","text":"Every city's settings live in site.toml at the root of its data repository. The commands read it from the current directory (or --site=FILE), and a wrong value stops the build with a message naming the key.\n\nslug = \"oslo\"\nname = \"Tangokalender | Oslo\"\ncity = \"Oslo\"\nsite_url = \"https://tango.oslo.no\"\nrepo_url = \"https://github.com/Tangokalender/tangokalender.github.io\"\nog_image = \"assets/og-image.png\"\n\n[map]\ncenter = [59.9139, 10.7522]\nzoom = 12\n\n[geocode]\ncountrycodes = \"no\"","title":"site.toml"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/site-config/#Keys","page":"site.toml","text":"The table is generated from the schema, schema/site.schema.json.\n\nusing TangoKalender, JSON, Markdown\ns=JSON.parsefile(TangoKalender.SITE_SCHEMA_FILE); req=Set(s[\"required\"])\nrows=String[]\nrow(k,p)=push!(rows,\"| `$k` | $(k in req ? \"yes\" : \"\") | $(replace(get(p,\"description\",\"\"),\"|\"=>\"\\\\|\")) |\")\nfor (k,p) in s[\"properties\"]\n if k in (\"map\",\"geocode\")\n  for (k2,p2) in p[\"properties\"]; row(\"$k.$k2\",p2); end\n elseif k!=\"texts\"\n  row(k,p)\n end\nend\nrow(\"texts.nb / .en / .es\",s[\"properties\"][\"texts\"])\nMarkdown.parse(\"| Key | Required | Meaning |\\n|:--|:--|:--|\\n\"*join(rows,\"\\n\"))\n  Key                  Required Meaning                                                                                                          \n  –––––––––––––––––––– –––––––– –––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––\n  \u001b[36mslug\u001b[39m                 yes      Short id of the site, e.g. oslo.                                                                                 \n  \u001b[36mname\u001b[39m                 yes      Site name in titles, feeds and previews, e.g. «Tangokalender | Oslo».                                            \n  \u001b[36mcity\u001b[39m                 yes      The city: default venue city, texts and geocoding.                                                               \n  \u001b[36msite_url\u001b[39m             yes      Where the site is published (may include a path), e.g. https://tango.oslo.no or https://example.github.io/bergen.\n  \u001b[36mrepo_url\u001b[39m             yes      The data repo with the issue forms.                                                                              \n  \u001b[36mog_image\u001b[39m                      Link-preview image (1200×630 PNG), relative to site.toml. Default: the package's generic image.                  \n  \u001b[36mmap.center\u001b[39m                    [lat, lon] shown when no event has a position.                                                                   \n  \u001b[36mmap.zoom\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                       \n  \u001b[36mgeocode.countrycodes\u001b[39m          Nominatim countrycodes, e.g. no.                                                                                 \n  \u001b[36mgeocode.viewbox\u001b[39m               Nominatim viewbox lon1,lat1,lon2,lat2 to prefer results in the city.                                             \n  \u001b[36mtexts.nb / .en / .es\u001b[39m          UI strings that replace the package's defaults, per language, keyed like src/i18n.jl (_T), e.g. site.tagline.    ","title":"Keys"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/site-config/#Changing-texts","page":"site.toml","text":"Any text on the site can be replaced per language under [texts.nb], [texts.en] or [texts.es], keyed like the package's strings in src/i18n.jl. {city} and {CITY} (upper case) are replaced by the city:\n\n[texts.nb]\n\"site.subtitle\" = \"Milongaer, practicaer og kurs i {city} og omegn\"\n[texts.en]\n\"site.subtitle\" = \"Milongas, practicas and classes in and around {city}\"","title":"Changing texts"},{"category":"section","location":"maintainers/site-config/#Norway-only","page":"site.toml","text":"All sites share Norwegian time (Europe/Oslo), prices in kroner and the Norwegian issue forms, so a city outside Norway would need changes in the package.","title":"Norway only"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/development/#Development-and-releases","page":"Development and releases","text":"julia --project=. -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.instantiate(); Pkg.test()'","title":"Development and releases"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/development/#Tests","page":"Development and releases","text":"The tests run as a test site: test/fixtures/site/ holds a site.toml and a frozen copy of the Oslo data, so they don't change when the real calendar does. test/runtests.jl sets that site; other sites in the tests (e.g. Bergen under a path) set their own.\nTests that depend on today's date pin it (today=, --today=).\nThe JavaScript tests run in Node and a real browser test runs in headless Chrome; both are skipped when the tool is missing (GitHub's runners have them).\nThe «site URL drift» test fails on any site URL written into src/ or templates/.","title":"Tests"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/development/#Precompile-workload","page":"Development and releases","text":"src/precompile.jl runs the CLI commands on a temporary tree during precompilation, so a CLI run takes about 2 s instead of about 30 s. Add new commands or slow first-use paths there.","title":"Precompile workload"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/development/#The-stand-alone-tangoedit","page":"Development and releases","text":"bin/build_tangoedit.sh compiles app/tangoedit.jl with JuliaC (--trim=safe) into build/tangoedit/. .github/workflows/tangoedit.yml builds it on Linux, Windows and macOS monthly and on every release tag, and attaches the archives to the GitHub release.","title":"The stand-alone tangoedit"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/development/#Documentation","page":"Development and releases","text":"julia --project=docs -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.instantiate()'\njulia --project=docs docs/make.jl          # → docs/build/index.html\n\nTables (event fields, site.toml keys) and the command reference are generated from the schemas and the usage texts. .github/workflows/docs.yml builds the docs on pull requests and publishes them from main (dev) and release tags (stable).","title":"Documentation"},{"category":"section","location":"dev/development/#Releases","page":"Development and releases","text":"Bump version in Project.toml, commit, tag vX.Y.Z, push both.\nThe tag builds the tangoedit binaries and the stable docs.\nEach city moves its pin (see Workflows and upgrades); the page footer shows the version.\n\nLint workflows with actionlint after editing them.","title":"Releases"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/tangotui/#Interactive-editor-(experimental)","page":"Interactive editor (experimental)","text":"warning: Experimental, Julia only\nTangoTUI is an experimental full-screen editor. It needs Julia (1.12 or newer) and a clone of this repository: it is not part of the stand-alone tangoedit download, because the terminal library it uses, Tachikoma.jl, can't be compiled into one. The screens are in Norwegian only for now. How it looks and works may still change; for anything that matters, check the result with git diff before you commit.\n\n(Image: TangoTUI: searching for a venue, opening a weekly milonga, changing the price for all later dates (invented events))\n\nTangoTUI edits one event at a time in a form, so you needn't know field names, JSON or event ids:\n\nIt starts on a list of the upcoming events. Type to search, as on the web page, and open an event with ↑/↓ and Enter.\nEvery field is shown with its current value. Fields with a fixed set of values (type, status, music, text language) open a pick list, so only allowed values can be chosen.\nA preview card shows the event as the site will, with changes highlighted and the old value struck through.\nWhen you save a change to a date that has later dates, it asks whether the change applies to them too, but never to another organiser's events.\n\nFor changes to many events in one go, or without Julia, use tangoedit.","title":"Interactive editor (experimental)"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/tangotui/#Set-up-and-start","page":"Interactive editor (experimental)","text":"In a clone of your city's data repository (the folder with events/ and site.toml), with this repository cloned at PATH:\n\njulia --project=PATH/TangoTUI -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.instantiate()'    # once, and after updating PATH\n\njulia --project=PATH/TangoTUI -m TangoTUI                    # the list of upcoming events\njulia --project=PATH/TangoTUI -m TangoTUI --all              # … including past events\njulia --project=PATH/TangoTUI -m TangoTUI edit otra-2026-11-02     # straight to one event\njulia --project=PATH/TangoTUI -m TangoTUI new                # a blank form\njulia --project=PATH/TangoTUI -m TangoTUI new series:otra    # a copy of the series' latest event, on a new date\n\nedit takes the same search terms as tangoedit (series:otra, type:class, venue:sentralen). When several events match, or none, it opens the list searching for them.","title":"Set up and start"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/tangotui/#The-list","page":"Interactive editor (experimental)","text":"Key \nletters search: every word must match, in the title (any language), venue, address, organiser, DJ, teachers, description, date, weekday, id or series; key:text searches one field\n↑ ↓, PgUp PgDn, Enter choose an event and open it\nCtrl-A also show past events (press again for upcoming only)\nCtrl-N a new, blank event\nCtrl-K a copy of the selected event on a new date (the date field opens first)\nEsc clear the search; on an empty search, quit","title":"The list"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/tangotui/#The-form","page":"Interactive editor (experimental)","text":"Key \n↑ ↓, Tab, PgUp PgDn choose a field\nEnter edit the field; Enter saves it, Tab saves and goes to the next, Esc cancels\nin a pick list ↑ ↓ to move, Space to tick (where several are allowed), Enter to choose\nDel clear the field\nCtrl-S save the event\nEsc back to the list (asks first if there are unsaved changes)\n\nA field that breaks a rule of the event format is marked ! in red, with the reason below the form; saving is refused until it's fixed. Some fields take short forms:\n\nDato: 2026-11-04 or 04.11.2026. A new date moves the end along, and the file moves to the new date's folder.\nStarttid: 20:00; empty for events without a time (festivals).\nSlutt: 23:30, or a time before the start for after midnight (01:30); 2026-11-08 for an event over several days, or 2026-11-08 18:00. Summer and winter time are handled.\nLærere: names separated by commas. Pris: whole kroner (150 or 150 kr).\nTittel: the event's own name, without the organiser (it has its own field and is shown in the list).\n\nA new event gets the id <series or title>-YYYY-MM-DD, like events from the submission forms.","title":"The form"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/tangotui/#The-same-change-on-several-dates","page":"Interactive editor (experimental)","text":"When you save a change to an event that has later dates, TangoTUI asks:\n\na: all later dates of the event's series, from this date on;\nu: all later events of the search you opened the event from (offered only when the list was filtered);\nd: only this date;\nEsc: cancel; nothing is saved.\n\nOnly the fields you changed are copied, never the date. A new start or end time is set on each date with the right summer or winter time, and an end some days later keeps its length. The question lists the dates, and marks those that had their own value (for example a special price) that would be overwritten.\n\nGuardrail: only events with the same organiser as the event you edit are changed. Events by other organisers in the series or the search are left alone and listed as skipped. All files are written together: if the check of the event tree fails, none of them are.","title":"The same change on several dates"},{"category":"section","location":"editors/tangotui/#After-saving","page":"Interactive editor (experimental)","text":"Saving writes the event files in their own key order and sets last_verified to today. TangoTUI never commits: when you quit, it lists the files it saved. Review and commit them as usual:\n\ngit diff\ngit add events && git commit -m \"Onsdagsmilonga: ny pris fra 28. oktober\"\ngit push\n\nThe animation above is made by bin/make_tui_demo.jl from TangoTUI's real screens, on invented events.","title":"After saving"}]
}
